  <data name="txtPurpose.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The main purpose of the game is to fight the opponent and decrease his health to 0, before the opponent decreases the player's health to 0. The outcome of the battle entirely depends on the player's choice of weapon and how they choose to fight the opponent. Which would consist of a choice of 8 weapons during the main menu (before the battle), with an additional 3 abilities when attacking the opponent. To elaborate, the weapons consist of a battle axe, bow &amp; arrow, crossbow, dagger, javelin, long sword, spear and warhammer. The 3 abilities consist of light attack, heavy attack and heal.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="richTextBox1.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>First, you will need to choose the desired weapon within the main menu. The weapons will be listed below the screen withn the main menu, in the form of buttons. These buttons may only be used once due to the fact only one weapon is needed to carry out the battle. CAUTION: Be aware that choosing weapons that has very high damage will also increase your health loss, so be careful when picking a weapon that would seem to kill the opponent quickly since it could also kill you quickly

Secondly, after choosing the weapon, you can click battle. This will initiate the battle screen and you can now start fighting the opponent. Furthermore, do not wait for the opponent to attack you as it only attacks when you attack it. 

During the Battle, attack the opponent using the given actions. The Given actions consist of a "light attack" and a "heavy attack" which have the sould purpose of damaging the enemy, however the enemy will also do twice the amount of damage that you do, so be extremely cautious when deciding to attack quickly.

After the Battle you will either get a Win screen or a Lose screen, which you can either improve your gameplay style by choosing a different weapon, or you can try a different combination of attacks to defeat the enemy. To play the game again, you will need to press "New Game" button to reset the buttons so they could be used again. </value>
  </data>
